According to Article 16 of the Ghanaian Constitution, "forced labour" does not include:

(a) any labour required as a result of a sentence or order of a court;

(b) any labour required of a member of a disciplined force or service as their duties, or in the case of a person who has conscientious objections to service as a member of the Armed Forces of Ghana, any labour which that person is required by law to perform in place of such service;

(c) any labour required during any period when Ghana is at war or in the event of an emergency or calamity that threatens the life and well-being of the community, to the extent that the requirement of such labour is reasonably justifiable in the circumstances;

(d) any labour reasonably required as part of normal communal or other civic obligations.

